1
00:00:14,447 --> 00:00:18,076
What? You want to see him?

2
00:00:19,319 --> 00:00:20,047
Yeah.

3
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,779
Why do you want to see him?

4
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:25,518
There's nothing interesting about him.

5
00:00:25,592 --> 00:00:27,526
That's right. It's a waste of time.

6
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,685
Just tell me!

7
00:00:30,263 --> 00:00:32,231
I heard that he's here.

8
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:35,524
The Shinigami who went down
to the Human World

9
00:00:35,602 --> 00:00:37,263
and did some interesting things.

10
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:18,969
Who is it?

11
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:23,579
I've come to see you.
I want you to tell me your story.

12
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:25,282
Story?

13
00:01:25,485 --> 00:01:27,180
I won't ask you to do it for free.

14
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:38,754
I would have liked it
if it was a little juicier...

15
00:01:43,069 --> 00:01:45,196
I want to go to the lower world.

16
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:48,073
I'm sick of this stagnant world.

17
00:01:48,408 --> 00:01:51,844
I heard that the Human World is fun.

18
00:01:56,583 --> 00:02:00,883
It's no fun watching guys
who complain about a dull world.

19
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:03,855
It's fun watching a guy
who foolishly thinks that...

20
00:02:03,923 --> 00:02:06,483
he can change the world.

21
00:02:09,596 --> 00:02:14,260
Fine. I was getting bored, anyway.
I'll tell you my story.

22
00:02:15,768 --> 00:02:17,736
This is for that gross apple.

23
00:02:18,538 --> 00:02:21,996
This is a story of a human...

24
00:02:22,075 --> 00:02:25,602
who tried to change the world
and become God.

25
00:02:32,085 --> 00:02:37,455
Someone's got to do it...
Things are no good as they are!

26
00:02:39,025 --> 00:02:42,222
Each day... repeats... itself.

27
00:02:43,196 --> 00:02:48,065
It would be better for the world
if everyone was dead!

28
00:02:49,135 --> 00:02:51,399
That's right. The world is corrupt.

29
00:02:53,039 --> 00:02:55,030
Those who are corrupt
are better off dead!

30
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:59,072
I'm going to... change the world...

31
00:03:00,246 --> 00:03:01,804
with the Death Note!

32
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:06,275
I'm going to wipe out evildoers.

33
00:03:06,886 --> 00:03:09,377
Yes, I'm cleansing the world!

34
00:03:09,923 --> 00:03:12,323
Those who have committed
terrible crimes...

35
00:03:12,392 --> 00:03:14,019
will succumb to heart attacks...

36
00:03:15,128 --> 00:03:18,154
Even an idiot will be able to figure out
that someone is behind it.

37
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:21,834
I'm going to let everyone
know of my existence!

38
00:03:22,902 --> 00:03:24,631
The power to fight evil!

39
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:29,675
Justice served!

40
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:48,717
If I do that, the world will be
a better place.

41
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:53,096
And I will create a world populated
only by kind, honest people

42
00:03:53,166 --> 00:03:55,498
who have received my approval.

43
00:03:56,869 --> 00:03:58,131
And I...

44
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:02,531
will become
the god of the new world.

45
00:04:03,009 --> 00:04:06,342
Death Note: Relight
Visions of a God

46
00:04:22,395 --> 00:04:24,226
Really? You went to see that?

47
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:25,821
It was a real waste of time.

48
00:04:25,898 --> 00:04:27,593
I want to get my money back.

49
00:05:04,404 --> 00:05:05,803
Death Note...

50
00:05:06,606 --> 00:05:08,574
Directly translated,
it means "notebook of death."

51
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:13,172
"How to use..."

52
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:18,383
"Those whose names are
written in this notebook will die."

53
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,212
How silly...

54
00:05:23,389 --> 00:05:25,619
This is really sick...

55
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:29,823
This isn't any better than
a chain letter...

56
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:33,393
"Those whose names are written
in this notebook will die"?

57
00:05:43,376 --> 00:05:46,777
Jeez... something's wrong
with me, too...

58
00:06:22,382 --> 00:06:25,351
Welcome home!
You're home early, Light.

59
00:06:25,852 --> 00:06:26,546
Yeah.

60
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:29,287
I'm home. Mom.

61
00:06:32,291 --> 00:06:35,089
Oh... The results of
the national mock exam?

62
00:06:35,328 --> 00:06:36,420
Quickly!

63
00:06:37,463 --> 00:06:38,259
Here.

64
00:06:38,798 --> 00:06:40,823
Oh my, number one again!

65
00:06:41,267 --> 00:06:43,030
You really worked hard,
didn't you, Light?!

66
00:06:43,269 --> 00:06:44,293
Yeah.

67
00:06:44,504 --> 00:06:46,995
Well, I'm going to be studying,
so don't bother me.

68
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,366
All right.

69
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:51,938
Oh, Light. Do you want anything?

70
00:06:52,011 --> 00:06:53,308
I'll get you whatever you want.

71
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:55,604
Nothing in particular, Mom.

72
00:06:58,785 --> 00:07:00,685
I already have what I want...

73
00:07:20,039 --> 00:07:21,631
I see you like it.

74
00:07:29,348 --> 00:07:31,282
Why are you so surprised?

75
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:33,881
I'm Ryuk, a Shinigami.

76
00:07:33,953 --> 00:07:35,784
I'm the one who dropped
that notebook.

77
00:07:36,422 --> 00:07:38,253
Judging by the way you were acting...

78
00:07:38,324 --> 00:07:41,725
I think you already know that
that's no ordinary notebook.

79
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:49,393
A Shinigami, huh..?

80
00:07:53,706 --> 00:07:55,901
I'm not surprised, Ryuk.

81
00:07:56,976 --> 00:07:57,943
No...

82
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:00,802
I've been waiting for you, Ryuk...

83
00:08:01,714 --> 00:08:02,646
Oh?

84
00:08:03,583 --> 00:08:08,486
I've had my doubts whether
the Shinigami notebook was real...

85
00:08:08,554 --> 00:08:13,685
But after seeing all sorts of things,
I'm confident in my actions...

86
00:08:14,594 --> 00:08:18,428
I see... You surprise me...

87
00:08:19,031 --> 00:08:22,523
I've heard that the Death Note
has appeared in the Human World

88
00:08:22,602 --> 00:08:24,900
many times in the past.

89
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:29,232
But you're the first who's done
this much in just five days.

90
00:08:29,308 --> 00:08:31,708
Most people would have been too scared
to write this many names...

91
00:08:32,445 --> 00:08:34,208
I'm prepared, Ryuk.

92
00:08:34,814 --> 00:08:36,714
I used the notebook
with the knowledge

93
00:08:36,782 --> 00:08:37,942
that it belonged to a Shinigami.

94
00:08:38,217 --> 00:08:39,684
And now a Shinigami has come...

95
00:08:40,453 --> 00:08:43,422
What are you going to do to me?
Are you going to take my soul?

96
00:08:44,390 --> 00:08:48,952
Hm? What are you talking about?
Is that what humans think we're like?

97
00:08:50,029 --> 00:08:52,259
I won't do anything to you.

98
00:08:53,599 --> 00:08:55,965
As soon as the notebook
lands in the Human World.

99
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:58,060
it becomes a part of it.

100
00:08:58,638 --> 00:09:01,732
In other words.
it belongs to you.

101
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:04,002
It's... mine..?

102
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:06,936
If you don't want it,
pass it to another human.

103
00:09:07,513 --> 00:09:11,643
When you do,
I'll erase your memories of it.

104
00:09:12,285 --> 00:09:16,551
Then there really is no price
for using the Death Note?

105
00:09:17,490 --> 00:09:19,219
If anything... the pain and fear

106
00:09:19,292 --> 00:09:23,456
that only someone who used
the Death Note would know...

107
00:09:25,097 --> 00:09:26,860
And when you die...

108
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:31,269
I'll write your name
in my notebook...

109
00:09:32,805 --> 00:09:35,330
Don't think that someone
who's used the Death Note

110
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:38,400
can go to heaven or hell.

111
00:09:39,946 --> 00:09:40,935
That's all.

112
00:09:46,152 --> 00:09:48,177
Look forward to that when you die.

113
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:54,385
This week alone. there have been
52 victims that we know of.

114
00:09:54,694 --> 00:09:56,685
They all died of heart attacks.

115
00:09:57,029 --> 00:10:00,658
There are probably some criminals
whose deaths aren't confirmed.

116
00:10:01,367 --> 00:10:03,767
- They were all criminals who...
- It's already started, Bureau Chief.

117
00:10:03,836 --> 00:10:05,133
probably would have been executed.

118
00:10:05,237 --> 00:10:07,137
- Yeah, I had a call from headquarters.
- Perhaps we shouldn't concern ourselves.

119
00:10:07,406 --> 00:10:08,430
How stupid!

120
00:10:08,507 --> 00:10:10,668
It doesn't matter if they're major criminals
or death row inmates.

121
00:10:10,743 --> 00:10:11,971
Murder is murder.

122
00:10:12,044 --> 00:10:14,274
We aren't sure that
it was murder yet.

123
00:10:14,347 --> 00:10:17,111
How can over a hundred people dying
of heart attacks be a coincidence?!

124
00:10:17,216 --> 00:10:21,380
There's nothing we can learn
from the way they've died.

125
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:25,288
I agree! It would be different if
they had been stabbed with knifes!

126
00:10:25,825 --> 00:10:29,192
We have to get L to help us!

127
00:10:33,766 --> 00:10:36,200
Bureau Chief. who's L?

128
00:10:36,402 --> 00:10:39,428
Oh, this is your first time at
an Interpol meeting, isn't it?

129
00:10:39,939 --> 00:10:44,273
No one knows L's name,
location, or even what he looks like.

130
00:10:44,944 --> 00:10:48,903
Furthermore. he solves
any case no matter how difficult.

131
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:51,916
He's solved many of
the world's unsolved cases.

132
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:55,545
He's one of the world's secret elite
and last hope...

133
00:10:55,621 --> 00:10:57,111
Something like that...

134
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:03,762
But L is an arrogant person
who only takes cases he's interested in!

135
00:11:04,096 --> 00:11:07,930
That's right.
And we have no way of contacting him!

136
00:11:08,234 --> 00:11:10,099
L is already on the move.

137
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:21,969
L has already begun
to investigate this case.

138
00:11:22,548 --> 00:11:23,913
W-Watari...

139
00:11:24,050 --> 00:11:25,483
Huh? Watari..?

140
00:11:25,885 --> 00:11:28,479
The only man who can contact L.

141
00:11:29,055 --> 00:11:31,853
Of course. no one knows
Watari's identity either...

142
00:11:32,291 --> 00:11:33,815
Please be silent.

143
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,492
I shall let you hear L's voice
right now.

144
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,859
Members of Interpol...

145
00:11:44,804 --> 00:11:45,793
I am L.

146
00:11:50,276 --> 00:11:52,301
The Legend of Kira the Savior...

147
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:55,245
That's pretty cool...
Are they referring to you?

148
00:11:55,514 --> 00:11:59,143
Yeah. it seems "Kira" comes
from the word "killer."

149
00:11:59,685 --> 00:12:01,482
I don't really like that...

150
00:12:01,787 --> 00:12:04,585
But the world already
knows me as Kira.

151
00:12:05,257 --> 00:12:09,216
If you do an internet search on Kira,
you'll find thousands of pages like this.

152
00:12:09,962 --> 00:12:11,793
Television and newspapers
have only reported

153
00:12:11,864 --> 00:12:15,561
The Deepening Mystery...
A Sensation is Called Accident
Reconsidering the Investigative System
Mysterious Deaths Continue
the successive bizarre deaths
of vicious criminals.

154
00:12:16,335 --> 00:12:20,066
But everyone in
the world can sense it.

155
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:22,707
That there's someone
who's seeking justice.

156
00:12:23,375 --> 00:12:24,342
Oh?

157
00:12:25,511 --> 00:12:26,773
This is good...

158
00:12:27,146 --> 00:12:29,671
Everything's going according
to plan.

159
00:12:30,516 --> 00:12:32,916
We interrupt our program
to bring you

160
00:12:32,985 --> 00:12:37,251
a special live broadcast
from Interpol.

161
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:38,890
Huh? What's this?

162
00:12:39,358 --> 00:12:40,791
Interpol..?

163
00:12:41,293 --> 00:12:42,521
We're about to begin.

164
00:12:43,896 --> 00:12:46,228
I am Lind L. Taylor,

165
00:12:46,298 --> 00:12:49,734
the only person who can move
the entire world's police.

166
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:52,503
I am otherwise known as "L."

167
00:12:52,972 --> 00:12:55,372
Wh-Who is he..?

168
00:12:56,108 --> 00:12:57,575
It's finally begun...

169
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:01,606
Someone has been systematically
murdering criminals.

170
00:13:02,248 --> 00:13:04,307
This is unforgivable.

171
00:13:04,483 --> 00:13:06,747
It is one of the greatest
criminal acts in history.

172
00:13:06,819 --> 00:13:09,287
Therefore, I intend to apprehend
the person responsible for these crimes...

173
00:13:09,355 --> 00:13:12,449
the person known as "Kira."

174
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:14,885
He says he's going to catch you.

175
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:18,293
What an idiot.
He can't catch me.

176
00:13:19,098 --> 00:13:20,588
I have a Death Note.

177
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:24,796
As long as I have this notebook,
I won't leave any proof behind.

178
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:27,731
It's impossible to catch me.

179
00:13:29,542 --> 00:13:32,409
The police are getting involved
and this guy making an appearance...

180
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:33,843
Everything's going according to plan.

181
00:13:34,213 --> 00:13:39,810
Kira, I have a pretty good idea of
why you're doing this.

182
00:13:40,719 --> 00:13:44,052
But what you're doing is evil!

183
00:13:46,125 --> 00:13:48,184
I'm evil?

184
00:13:50,429 --> 00:13:51,726
I am justice!

185
00:13:51,797 --> 00:13:54,095
I protect the weak who fear evil.

186
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:56,157
I am the man who
will become...

187
00:13:56,235 --> 00:13:57,702
the god of the ideal, new world!

188
00:13:57,803 --> 00:13:59,771
And all those who oppose this god...

189
00:13:59,939 --> 00:14:01,201
are evil!

190
00:14:03,742 --> 00:14:05,505
You're too foolish. L...

191
00:14:05,878 --> 00:14:07,709
It would have been
a little more interesting

192
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:09,941
if you'd have been
a little smarter...

193
00:14:25,097 --> 00:14:27,964
I'll show you what happens
if you defy me...

194
00:14:28,467 --> 00:14:31,800
The whole world is watching, L.

195
00:14:36,308 --> 00:14:37,434
Five more seconds.

196
00:14:37,977 --> 00:14:41,538
4... 3... 2... 1...

197
00:14:54,593 --> 00:14:56,891
What's wrong?
Why don't you say something?!

198
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:03,165
Unbelievable...

199
00:15:04,103 --> 00:15:07,664
I was just testing to make sure,
but I didn't think it was possible...

200
00:15:08,274 --> 00:15:12,643
Kira... you can kill by indirect means...

201
00:15:14,046 --> 00:15:17,072
Had I not seen it with my own eyes,
I would have never believed it.

202
00:15:18,050 --> 00:15:19,449
Listen closely, Kira.

203
00:15:19,518 --> 00:15:24,854
If you have killed the man
on your screen, Lind L. Taylor,

204
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:28,451
you just killed a man who was
to be executed today at this time.

205
00:15:29,228 --> 00:15:30,593
Not me.

206
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:31,821
What..?!

207
00:15:31,897 --> 00:15:34,092
It hasn't been reported
on television or the internet.

208
00:15:34,633 --> 00:15:37,295
He's a criminal that the police
caught in secret.

209
00:15:37,836 --> 00:15:42,102
Even you weren't able
to gather information on him.

210
00:15:44,343 --> 00:15:45,537
He tricked you.

211
00:15:46,245 --> 00:15:49,442
But I... L, do exist!

212
00:15:50,683 --> 00:15:52,514
Now try to kill me!

213
00:15:53,385 --> 00:15:55,216
Th-That bastard..!

214
00:15:55,788 --> 00:15:56,846
What's wrong?

215
00:15:56,922 --> 00:15:58,719
- Hurry up and do it!
- What is this?! This is incredible!

216
00:15:58,891 --> 00:16:00,756
- Quickly! Try to kill me!
- Are you trying to get yourself killed, L?!

217
00:16:00,826 --> 00:16:01,724
What's going on?!

218
00:16:01,827 --> 00:16:04,591
What's wrong?
Kill me right now!

219
00:16:04,763 --> 00:16:07,698
- Kill me right now!
- It's Kira versus L!

220
00:16:09,034 --> 00:16:10,899
Can't you do it?

221
00:16:13,872 --> 00:16:16,363
It seems that you can't kill me...

222
00:16:17,242 --> 00:16:19,335
There are some people
you can't kill...

223
00:16:20,112 --> 00:16:22,137
You've given me a good hint.

224
00:16:22,381 --> 00:16:26,477
In return, I'll tell you
something interesting.

225
00:16:27,119 --> 00:16:30,782
I said that this broadcast was
being aired live around the world...

226
00:16:30,856 --> 00:16:33,984
But actually, was only broadcast
in Japan's Kanto region.

227
00:16:35,227 --> 00:16:37,127
I was planning on airing this broadcast
in other regions at different times,

228
00:16:37,196 --> 00:16:39,187
but it seems that there's no need
for that anymore.

229
00:16:39,798 --> 00:16:42,767
You're in Kanto right now.

230
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:45,693
L's pretty good.

231
00:16:46,271 --> 00:16:50,571
I never thought that things
would go quite so well.

232
00:16:50,776 --> 00:16:55,611
But, Kira, it seems that it might
not be too long till I get you executed.

233
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:58,578
I knew it... L is just as
I had expected he would be...

234
00:16:58,784 --> 00:17:02,083
Yes. He's proved Kira's existence,
that the killings took place,

235
00:17:02,154 --> 00:17:04,748
and that Kira's in Japan...

236
00:17:05,791 --> 00:17:11,127
Kira, I'm very interested in
what method you use to kill.

237
00:17:12,097 --> 00:17:13,257
But I'll find that out...

238
00:17:13,332 --> 00:17:15,766
...when I catch you.

239
00:17:16,769 --> 00:17:19,294
Until we meet again, Kira.

240
00:17:32,451 --> 00:17:34,919
Light, do you have a minute?

241
00:17:35,287 --> 00:17:38,222
Ryuk, I told you not to talk
to me outside.

242
00:17:38,857 --> 00:17:40,415
How many times do I have
to remind you?

243
00:17:40,626 --> 00:17:42,856
Then I'll just talk to you.

244
00:17:43,362 --> 00:17:45,830
Close your ears if
you don't want to listen.

245
00:17:49,334 --> 00:17:52,667
Someone's been following you
for a while now.

246
00:18:25,304 --> 00:18:26,396
I'm L.

247
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:28,004
This man is?

248
00:18:28,707 --> 00:18:30,698
He looks different from
what I imagined...

249
00:18:34,546 --> 00:18:36,309
I'm Yagami of the Police Department.

250
00:18:36,982 --> 00:18:38,244
Oh. I'm Matsuda.

251
00:18:38,317 --> 00:18:39,249
I'm Aizawa.

252
00:18:39,318 --> 00:18:40,250
I'm Mogi.

253
00:18:40,319 --> 00:18:41,251
I'm Ukita.

254
00:18:42,888 --> 00:18:46,016
I'm sorry we're late.
These five are the current...

255
